            "tags": [
                [
                    "param",
                    "begin The starting value."
                ],
                [
                    "param",
                    "end The value that serves as the stopping criterion. This value is not included in the range."
                ],
                [
                    "param",
                    "step The value to add to the current value at each iteration."
                ],
                [
                    "returns",
                    "A range that goes through the numbers `begin`, `begin + step`,\n`begin + 2 * step`, `...`, up to and excluding ``end``.\n\nThe two-argument overloads have `step = 1`. If `begin < `end` && step <\n0` or `begin > `end` && step > 0` or `begin == `end``, then an empty range\nis returned. If `step == 0` then `begin == `end`` is an error.\n\nFor built-in types, the range returned is a random access range. For\nuser-defined types that support `++`, the range is an input\nrange.\n\n**`in` operator and `contains`::**\n``iota`` over an integral/pointer type defines the `in` operator from the right.\n`val in `iota`(...)` is `true` when `val` occurs in the range. When present, it takes\n`step` into account - `val` won't be considered\ncontained if it falls between two consecutive elements of the range.\nThe `contains` method does the same as `in`, but from the left-hand side."
                ]
            ],
